odyssey.cy.cry=§bPolyphemus: §f"Father Poseidon, they blinded me! Vengeance, father, vengeance for pain... Poseidon, vengeance for pain!"
odyssey.cy.blind_hint=§7He is blind. He counts his sheep by feeling their wool — hide among the flock.
odyssey.cy.hidden=§7Polyphemus runs his hands over the wool of his sheep... he does not find you.
odyssey.cy.devour=§4Polyphemus snatches you up and lifts you to his mouth...
odyssey.cy.kick=§cA kick from Polyphemus sends you flying.
odyssey.cy.stomp=§cThe ground shakes under Polyphemus's foot.
odyssey.lae.child_laugh=§7You ask the armoured child for hospitality. The child only laughs at you.
odyssey.lae.child_scream=§7You ask again, more seriously. §cThe child screams and runs. Something enormous moves in the fog...
odyssey.lae.emerge=§7Giants in silver armour emerge from the fog.
odyssey.lae.impale=§cThe glaive lifts you off your feet and flings you into the air.
odyssey.lae.crush=§cThe mace crushes the ground beneath you.
odyssey.circe.scream=§5Circe screams at the sight of armoured strangers.
odyssey.circe.no_armor=§5Circe will feed you — on condition that you leave your armour outside.
odyssey.circe.stew=§5Circe sets a bowl of stew before you.
odyssey.circe.pliable=§dYou devour the stew with a grotesque hunger... and feel strangely pliable.
odyssey.circe.molded=§5Circe works your flesh and bones as a potter works clay. Your scream becomes a squeal.
odyssey.circe.human=§aYou are human again.
odyssey.circe.seized=§5You grab Circe's sister. Circe stands down.
odyssey.circe.claims=§5Circe says she only made your men what they really are — brutal and savage. Reluctantly, she turns them back.
odyssey.circe.hades=§5To reach Ithaca, she tells you, you must cross the river Oceanus into Hades.
odyssey.circe.counsel=§5Circe: to reach Ithaca, you must cross the river Oceanus into Hades.
odyssey.siren.muffled=§7Wax in your ears: the song is only a muffled hum.
odyssey.siren.mast=§5Bound to the mast, you hear it all: everything you could ever want — and why you can never have it.
odyssey.siren.pull=§d♪ The Sirens' song draws you toward the rocks... ♪
odyssey.siren.dragged=§4The Sirens drag you under.
odyssey.siren.wax_on=§eYou press soft wax into your ears. The sound dulls away.
odyssey.siren.wax_off=§eThe wax has worked loose. You can hear again.
odyssey.scylla.snatch=§4Scylla's heads lunge out of the cliff and snatch their victims from the deck.
odyssey.scylla.devour=§4A head of Scylla hauls you up toward the cliff and chews.
odyssey.scylla.rend=§4Scylla tears through the ship.
odyssey.charybdis.drain=§3The sea is draining into Charybdis's throat!
odyssey.charybdis.surge=§3The whirlpool surges!
odyssey.hades.rise=§7The blood soaks into the black sand. The dead begin to rise.
odyssey.hades.sinon=§7Sinon's shade reproaches you for deceiving him — and reveals that Antinous manipulated him into taking his place in the Greek army.
odyssey.hades.agamemnon=§7Agamemnon's shade reveals that Clytemnestra murdered him on his return, in revenge for sacrificing their daughter Iphigenia to Artemis for fair seas.
odyssey.hades.tiresias=§fTiresias: "The Whirlpool in the sea takes all of your lives, the monster in the cliff only six."
odyssey.hades.fate=§7Tiresias foretells that, by divine will, only you will return home — and that your men will die if they kill the cattle of Apollo.
odyssey.hades.crew=§cThe shades rapidly approaching are your unburied crew. They want you to join them in their shame.
odyssey.hades.grasp=§cThe dead drag at you, wanting you to join them.
odyssey.zeus.storm=§6You have killed one of the cattle of Apollo. Zeus sends a storm.
odyssey.calypso.lotus=§bCalypso offers you a lotus flower.
odyssey.calypso.eaten=§bA peaceful haze settles over you. Your memories slip away.
odyssey.calypso.embrace=§bCalypso holds you close. For a moment you are at ease.
odyssey.athena.bless=§fAthena commands you to return home. You feel her protection settle over you.
odyssey.athena.vision=§fAthena appears in your hour of crisis: "Return home."
odyssey.horse.hide=§7You hide inside the Trojan Horse.
odyssey.horse.sally=§7The Greeks pour out of the horse.
odyssey.calypso.lotus_bar=§b+1 Lotus Flower §7(Next gift in 15s)
odyssey.calypso.lotus_cd=§7Calypso is gathering another Lotus Flower (%1s remaining)
odyssey.calypso.inv_full=§cYour inventory is full — free a slot to receive Calypso's Lotus Flower.
odyssey.comp.follow_on=§aCompanion is now following you.
odyssey.comp.follow_off=§eCompanion will guard this location.
odyssey.comp.warn.athena=§fAthena: §7"Stand firm, Odysseus — enemies close in!"
odyssey.comp.warn.calypso=§bCalypso: §7"Careful, my love — danger approaches!"
odyssey.comp.warn.circe=§5Circe: §7"Fools and monsters draw near. Let my hex slow their limbs."
odyssey.comp.assist.athena=§fAthena's Aegis shields and strengthens you!
odyssey.comp.assist.calypso=§bCalypso's island mist restores your strength!
odyssey.comp.assist.circe=§5Circe's hex weakens nearby enemies!
odyssey.ch.1=§6[Chapter I: Ogygia] §fHeld on Calypso's island, you must resist forgetfulness and begin your voyage home to Ithaca.
odyssey.ch.1.hint=§eObjective: §7Receive a Lotus from Calypso, then sail northwest to Troy (-150, -260).
odyssey.ch.2=§6[Chapter II: The Fall of Troy] §fRelive the night the Trojan Horse opened on the shores of Troy.
odyssey.ch.2.hint=§eObjective: §7Inspect the Trojan Horse at Troy (-150, -260) or sail east to Cyclops Island (300, -150).
odyssey.ch.3=§6[Chapter III: The Cave of Polyphemus] §fTrapped near Nestor's Cave, outwit the giant shepherd Polyphemus.
odyssey.ch.3.hint=§eObjective: §7Wait for nightfall on Cyclops Island (300, -150) and blind sleeping Polyphemus with the Burning Stake.
odyssey.ch.4=§6[Chapter IV: Telepylus] §fSail into the fog of Telepylus, land of Antiphates and the silver-armored Laestrygonians.
odyssey.ch.4.hint=§eObjective: §7Survive the Laestrygonian ambush at Telepylus (560, 60) and sail south to Aeaea (520, 360).
odyssey.ch.5=§6[Chapter V: Circe's Stronghold] §fConfront the sorceress Circe on the cliffs of Aeaea.
odyssey.ch.5.hint=§eObjective: §7Seize Circe's bird-sister on Aeaea (520, 360) so Circe yields and reveals the path to Hades.
odyssey.ch.6=§6[Chapter VI: Across Oceanus to Hades] §fSeek the blind prophet Tiresias on the black volcanic sands of Hades.
odyssey.ch.6.hint=§eObjective: §7Kill a sheep while standing on black sand in Hades (260, 520) to summon Sinon, Agamemnon, and Tiresias.
odyssey.ch.7=§6[Chapter VII: Song of the Sirens] §fSail past the mist-shrouded rocks of the Sirens without being dragged under.
odyssey.ch.7.hint=§eObjective: §7Use Wax to stop your ears and pass the Sirens (-40, 480) toward the Strait (-300, 380).
odyssey.ch.8=§6[Chapter VIII: Scylla, Charybdis & Thrinacia] §fBrave the six heads of Scylla and the whirlpool of Charybdis, and spare Apollo's cattle.
odyssey.ch.8.hint=§eObjective: §7Pass the Strait (-300, 380) and Thrinacia (-480, 130) to reach Ithaca (-420, -200).
odyssey.ch.9=§6[Chapter IX: Return to Ithaca] §fReclaim your kingdom alongside Telemachus and Penelope.
odyssey.ch.9.hint=§eObjective: §7Speak with Athena on Ithaca (-420, -200) to fulfill your homecoming.
odyssey.story.ogygia_intro=§bCalypso watches the tide on Ogygia. Every 15 seconds she offers a fresh Lotus of forgetfulness — yet Ithaca awaits.
odyssey.story.troy_intro=§7The massive wooden horse stands on the beach of Troy, where Sinon's ruse and Odysseus's strategy ended a ten-year war.
odyssey.story.horse_memory=§7Inside the timber belly of the Trojan Horse, you remember the silence before the midnight raid on Troy.
odyssey.story.cyclops_done=§aPolyphemus is blinded! Stay close to the wool of his sheep so he cannot feel you in the dark.
odyssey.story.aeaea_intro=§5On the wind-swept cliffs of Aeaea, Circe tends her cauldron while her sister perches on her shoulder.
odyssey.story.circe_done=§aCirce stands down and lifts her curse, pointing your ship toward the black sands of Hades.
odyssey.story.hades_intro=§7Across the river Oceanus lie the black sands of Hades. Sacrifice a sheep on the black sand to call forth the dead.
odyssey.story.hades_done=§aThe dead have spoken: Sinon, Agamemnon, and Tiresias have revealed the perils of the Strait and Thrinacia.
odyssey.story.sirens_intro=§dMist curls over the Sirens' rocks. Press Beeswax into your ears before their song pulls you into the sea.
odyssey.story.strait_intro=§3The Strait narrows between Charybdis's whirlpool and Scylla's cliff. Steer hard and do not linger!
odyssey.story.thrinacia_intro=§6The sacred cattle of Apollo graze on Thrinacia. Tiresias warned that slaying even one will bring Zeus's storm.
odyssey.story.ithaca_intro=§fThe rocky shores of Ithaca rise before you, where Penelope and Telemachus have held your house against Antinous and the suitors.
odyssey.story.ithaca_complete=§6§lHOMECOMING COMPLETE: §r§fWith Athena's blessing, Odysseus stands once more upon Ithaca!
odyssey.athena.guide.2=§fAthena: §7"Remember the stratagem of the Trojan Horse, then set your prow east toward Polyphemus's island (300, -150)."
odyssey.athena.guide.3=§fAthena: §7"Wait until Polyphemus sleeps at night, then drive the Burning Stake into his eye and hide among his sheep."
odyssey.athena.guide.5=§fAthena: §7"Do not let Circe mold you into swine. Seize the bird upon her shoulder and force her to name the way to Hades."
odyssey.athena.guide.6=§fAthena: §7"On the black sand of Hades (260, 520), offer the blood of a sheep so blind Tiresias may speak your fate."
odyssey.athena.guide.7=§fAthena: §7"Stop your ears with wax before the Sirens (-40, 480) sing of all you have lost."
odyssey.athena.guide.8=§fAthena: §7"Hold fast through Scylla and Charybdis (-300, 380), and do not touch Apollo's cattle on Thrinacia (-480, 130)."
odyssey.athena.guide.9=§fAthena: §7"You have returned to Ithaca (-420, -200). Stand with Telemachus and reclaim your house."
odyssey.calypso.guide.early=§bCalypso: §7"Why brave Poseidon's wrath when Ogygia is at peace? Take a Lotus every 15 seconds, or sneak-interact if you wish me to walk beside you."
odyssey.calypso.guide.late=§bCalypso: §7"Your heart is still set on Ithaca and Penelope. I will walk with you and mend your wounds while you journey."
odyssey.circe.guide.hades=§5Circe: §7"Sail southwest to Hades (260, 520) and spill a sheep's blood upon the black sand to summon Tiresias."
odyssey.circe.guide.strait=§5Circe: §7"Beyond the Sirens (-40, 480) lies the Strait (-300, 380): Charybdis swallows the whole ship, Scylla takes six."
