odyssey.ch.1.title=Twenty Years
odyssey.ch.1.story=§7Ithaca waits for a king who does not return. On Ogygia, Odysseus waits for a way home.
odyssey.ch.2.title=The Horse
odyssey.ch.2.story=§7The tale begins at Troy, on the night the wooden Horse was left on the beach.
odyssey.ch.3.title=The Shepherd's Cave
odyssey.ch.3.story=§7An island of goats and a cave too big for men.
odyssey.ch.4.title=Telepylus
odyssey.ch.4.story=§7A quiet harbour, and the giants who own it.
odyssey.ch.5.title=Circe
odyssey.ch.5.story=§7Smoke from a hall in the woods. The crew go to look.
odyssey.ch.6.title=The Land of the Dead
odyssey.ch.6.story=§7To learn the way home, Odysseus must ask the dead.
odyssey.ch.7.title=The Sirens
odyssey.ch.7.story=§7A song that has drowned every crew that heard it.
odyssey.ch.8.title=The Strait and the Sun's Cattle
odyssey.ch.8.story=§7Between the cliff and the whirlpool, then an island where hunger tests an oath.
odyssey.ch.9.title=Homecoming
odyssey.ch.9.story=§7Ithaca at last, in rags. A hall full of suitors, and a bow no one can string.
odyssey.end.sub=§7Chapter complete
odyssey.end.1=§7A galley on the beach. The goddess has kept her word: the way home is open.
odyssey.end.2=§7Troy burns. The long road home begins.
odyssey.end.3=§7The giant's cry follows them out to sea.
odyssey.end.4=§7Fewer ships leave Telepylus than arrived.
odyssey.end.5=§7Circe points the way: down, to the dead.
odyssey.end.6=§7The prophet has spoken. The road home runs past the Sirens.
odyssey.end.7=§7The song fades behind them. Ahead, the narrow water.
odyssey.end.8=§7Ithaca's cliffs rise out of the morning haze.
