odyssey.open.ithaca.title=§6ITHACA
odyssey.open.ithaca.sub=§7Twenty years after the war
odyssey.open.ithaca.1=§7The suitors have made the king's hall their own.
odyssey.open.ithaca.2=§7Mentor: §f"If no one will tell you what became of him, go and ask the ones who were there."
odyssey.open.ithaca.3=§7A small boat waits in the harbour.
odyssey.open.ogygia.title=§6OGYGIA
odyssey.open.ogygia.sub=§7An island at the edge of the sea
odyssey.open.ogygia.1=§7Seven years on this shore. The memory of home grows thin.
odyssey.open.ogygia.2=§7Calypso: §f"Stay. Here nothing ends."
odyssey.open.ogygia.3=§7Out on the water, a sail.
odyssey.finale.title=§6THE BOW
odyssey.finale.sub=§7The king is home
odyssey.finale.1=§7The string sings. The hall falls silent.
odyssey.finale.2=§7Odysseus: §f"Ithaca needs a king who stayed. That was always you, my son."
odyssey.finale.3=§7Two figures sail west into the evening.
odyssey.finale.end=§6§lTHE ODYSSEY
odyssey.finale.end.sub=§7Thank you for playing
odyssey.regroup=§7You join Odysseus as he tells the tale of the voyage — and live it at his side.
